IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc23-interpretation.l4 -- section 672.1 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: the definitions of Part XX.1 (Mental Disorder)
-- and the rule of reading in subsection (2). Layer 1 (the law, objectively); written from the text alone.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text. The French equivalents in parentheses
-- after a defined term are not text to encode and are not quoted as such.
--
-- HOW EACH TERM IS ANSWERED. Every term is a function `s 672.1(1) <term>` that answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--   JUST TRUE   the facts bring the case within the term, on the text's own words;
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words ("means", "where", "if", "only", a flat negative);
--   NOTHING     not covered: "includes" lists without closing the list, or the case is outside what the text limits itself to.
-- Every branch that answers JUST FALSE carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)` and every branch that answers NOTHING carries `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Facts are plain BOOLEAN inputs; a term that is the answer of another provision
-- of the Code is taken as an input named for that provision (PLAN.md section 3, rule R4).

§ `Section 672.1(1) -- Definitions ("In this Part,")`

-- accused includes a defendant in summary conviction proceedings and an accused in respect of whom a verdict of not criminally responsible has been rendered.
-- The base meaning (a person charged with an offence) is the word's ordinary sense; the definition only extends it.
-- src:13311 | accused includes a defendant in summary conviction proceedings and an accused in respect of whom a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered; (accusé)
@ref s 672.1(1) "accused" (src:13311)
GIVEN `a person charged with an offence, in the ordinary sense of the word` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a defendant in summary conviction proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an accused in respect of whom a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.1(1) accused` MEANS
    IF     `a person charged with an offence, in the ordinary sense of the word`
        OR `a defendant in summary conviction proceedings`
        OR `an accused in respect of whom a verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder has been rendered`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "accused includes"

-- assessment means an assessment by a medical practitioner or another person designated by the Attorney General as qualified to conduct it, of the mental
-- condition of the accused, under an assessment order made under section 672.11 or 672.121, and any incidental observation or examination of the accused.
-- src:13312 | assessment means an assessment by a medical practitioner or any other person who has been designated by the Attorney General as being qualified to conduct an assessment of the mental condition of the accused under an assessment order made under section 672.11 or 672.121, and any incidental observation or examination of the accused; (évaluation)
@ref s 672.1(1) "assessment" (src:13312)
GIVEN `it is an assessment by a medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an assessment by another person designated by the Attorney General as being qualified to conduct an assessment of the mental condition of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an assessment of the mental condition of the accused under an assessment order made under section 672.11 or 672.121` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an incidental observation or examination of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.1(1) assessment` MEANS
    IF     (    (   `it is an assessment by a medical practitioner`
                 OR `it is an assessment by another person designated by the Attorney General as being qualified to conduct an assessment of the mental condition of the accused`)
            AND `it is an assessment of the mental condition of the accused under an assessment order made under section 672.11 or 672.121`)
        OR `it is an incidental observation or examination of the accused`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "assessment means an assessment by a medical practitioner or any other person who has been designated by the Attorney General"

-- chairperson includes any alternate that the chairperson of a Review Board may designate to act on the chairperson's behalf.
-- The two limbs are separate facts. The function name below is the one PLAN.md section 6 gives for the seam that s 2 "videoconference" asks of this part;
-- PLAN.md types it BOOLEAN, but "includes" does not close the list, so the answer is a MAYBE BOOLEAN (the brief's rule governs: see NOTES.md, Seams).
-- src:13313 | chairperson includes any alternate that the chairperson of a Review Board may designate to act on the chairperson’s behalf; (président)
@ref s 672.1(1) "chairperson" (src:13313)
GIVEN `the person is the chairperson of a Review Board` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an alternate that the chairperson of a Review Board has designated to act on the chairperson’s behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.1(1) the issuer is the chairperson of a Review Board` MEANS
    IF `the person is the chairperson of a Review Board` OR `the person is an alternate that the chairperson of a Review Board has designated to act on the chairperson’s behalf`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "chairperson includes"

-- court includes a summary conviction court as defined in section 785, a judge, a justice and a judge of the court of appeal as defined in section 673.
-- src:13314 | court includes a summary conviction court as defined in section 785, a judge, a justice and a judge of the court of appeal as defined in section 673; (tribunal)
@ref s 672.1(1) "court" (src:13314)
GIVEN `it is a court, in the ordinary sense of the word` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a summary conviction court as defined in section 785` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a judge of the court of appeal as defined in section 673` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.1(1) court` MEANS
    IF     `it is a court, in the ordinary sense of the word`
        OR `it is a summary conviction court as defined in section 785`
        OR `it is a judge`
        OR `it is a justice`
        OR `it is a judge of the court of appeal as defined in section 673`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "court includes"

-- disposition means an order by a court or Review Board under section 672.54, an order by a court under section 672.58, or a finding by a court under subsection 672.64(1).
-- One declared type is shared by the later modules, so that a "kind of disposition" is said once.
-- src:13315 | disposition means an order made by a court or Review Board under section 672.54, an order made by a court under section 672.58 or a finding made by a court under subsection 672.64(1); (décision)
@ref s 672.1(1) "disposition" (src:13315)
DECLARE `s 672.1(1) kind of decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 672.1(1) an order made by a court or Review Board under section 672.54`
    `s 672.1(1) an order made by a court under section 672.58`
    `s 672.1(1) a finding made by a court under subsection 672.64(1)`
    `s 672.1(1) a decision of any other kind`

@ref s 672.1(1) "disposition" (src:13315)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 672.1(1) kind of decision`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.1(1) disposition` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 672.1(1) an order made by a court or Review Board under section 672.54` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 672.1(1) an order made by a court under section 672.58` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 672.1(1) a finding made by a court under subsection 672.64(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 672.1(1) a decision of any other kind` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "disposition means an order made by a court or Review Board under section 672.54"

-- dual status offender means an offender who is subject to a sentence of imprisonment for one offence and a custodial disposition under paragraph 672.54(c) for another.
-- src:13316 | dual status offender means an offender who is subject to a sentence of imprisonment in respect of one offence and a custodial disposition under paragraph 672.54(c) in respect of another offence; (contrevenant à double statut)
@ref s 672.1(1) "dual status offender" (src:13316)
GIVEN `the person is an offender` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to a sentence of imprisonment in respect of one offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is subject to a custodial disposition under paragraph 672.54(c) in respect of another offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.1(1) dual status offender` MEANS
    IF `the person is an offender` AND `the person is subject to a sentence of imprisonment in respect of one offence` AND `the person is subject to a custodial disposition under paragraph 672.54(c) in respect of another offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "dual status offender means an offender who is subject to a sentence of imprisonment in respect of one offence and a custodial disposition under paragraph 672.54(c) in respect of another offence"

-- high-risk accused means an accused who is found to be a high-risk accused by a court under subsection 672.64(1).
-- src:13317 | high-risk accused means an accused who is found to be a high-risk accused by a court under subsection 672.64(1); (accusé à haut risque)
@ref s 672.1(1) "high-risk accused" (src:13317)
GIVEN `the accused has been found to be a high-risk accused by a court under subsection 672.64(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.1(1) high-risk accused` MEANS
    IF `the accused has been found to be a high-risk accused by a court under subsection 672.64(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "high-risk accused means an accused who is found to be a high-risk accused by a court under subsection 672.64(1)"

-- hospital means a place in a province designated by the Minister of Health for the province for the custody, treatment or assessment of an accused for whom an assessment order, disposition or placement decision is made.
-- src:13318 | hospital means a place in a province that is designated by the Minister of Health for the province for the custody, treatment or assessment of an accused in respect of whom an assessment order, a disposition or a placement decision is made; (hôpital)
@ref s 672.1(1) "hospital" (src:13318)
GIVEN `it is a place in a province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is designated by the Minister of Health for the province for the custody, treatment or assessment of an accused in respect of whom an assessment order, a disposition or a placement decision is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.1(1) hospital` MEANS
    IF `it is a place in a province` AND `it is designated by the Minister of Health for the province for the custody, treatment or assessment of an accused in respect of whom an assessment order, a disposition or a placement decision is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "hospital means a place in a province that is designated by the Minister of Health for the province"

-- medical practitioner means a person who is entitled to practise medicine by the laws of a province.
-- src:13319 | medical practitioner means a person who is entitled to practise medicine by the laws of a province; (médecin)
@ref s 672.1(1) "medical practitioner" (src:13319)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to practise medicine by the laws of a province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.1(1) medical practitioner` MEANS
    IF `the person is entitled to practise medicine by the laws of a province`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "medical practitioner means a person who is entitled to practise medicine by the laws of a province"

-- party, in relation to proceedings of a court or Review Board to make or review a disposition, means (a) the accused, (b) the person in charge of the hospital, (c) an Attorney General
-- designated under 672.5(3), (d) an interested person designated under 672.5(4), (e) where the disposition is to be made by a court, the prosecutor.
-- Outside proceedings to make or review a disposition the definition does not speak (a scope limit with no "only"): NOTHING.
-- src:13320 | party, in relation to proceedings of a court or Review Board to make or review a disposition, means
-- src:13321 | (a) the accused,
-- src:13322 | (b) the person in charge of the hospital where the accused is detained or is to attend pursuant to an assessment order or a disposition,
-- src:13323 | (c) an Attorney General designated by the court or Review Board under subsection 672.5(3),
-- src:13324 | (d) any interested person designated by the court or Review Board under subsection 672.5(4), or
-- src:13325 | (e) where the disposition is to be made by a court, the prosecutor of the charge against the accused; (parties)
@ref s 672.1(1) "party"; s 672.1(1) "party"(a); s 672.1(1) "party"(b); s 672.1(1) "party"(c); s 672.1(1) "party"(d); s 672.1(1) "party"(e) (src:13320-13325)
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings of a court or Review Board to make or review a disposition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the accused` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `the person is in charge of the hospital where the accused is detained or is to attend pursuant to an assessment order or a disposition` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `the person is an Attorney General designated by the court or Review Board under subsection 672.5(3)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
      `the person is an interested person designated by the court or Review Board under subsection 672.5(4)` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
      `the person is the prosecutor of the charge against the accused` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e), second element
      `the disposition is to be made by a court` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e), first element
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.1(1) party` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are proceedings of a court or Review Board to make or review a disposition` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to proceedings of a court or Review Board to make or review a disposition"
        IF `the person is the accused` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is in charge of the hospital where the accused is detained or is to attend pursuant to an assessment order or a disposition` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is an Attorney General designated by the court or Review Board under subsection 672.5(3)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is an interested person designated by the court or Review Board under subsection 672.5(4)` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person is the prosecutor of the charge against the accused` AND `the disposition is to be made by a court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "party, in relation to proceedings of a court or Review Board to make or review a disposition, means"

-- placement decision means a decision by a Review Board under subsection 672.68(2) as to the place of custody of a dual status offender.
-- src:13326 | placement decision means a decision by a Review Board under subsection 672.68(2) as to the place of custody of a dual status offender; (ordonnance de placement)
@ref s 672.1(1) "placement decision" (src:13326)
GIVEN `it is a decision by a Review Board under subsection 672.68(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a decision as to the place of custody of a dual status offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.1(1) placement decision` MEANS
    IF `it is a decision by a Review Board under subsection 672.68(2)` AND `it is a decision as to the place of custody of a dual status offender`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "placement decision means a decision by a Review Board under subsection 672.68(2)"

-- prescribed means prescribed by regulations made by the Governor in Council under section 672.95. The regulations are not among the sources: whether they prescribe the thing is an input.
