-- verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder means a verdict that the accused committed the act or made the omission that formed the basis of the offence charged but is not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder.
-- src:13329 | verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder means a verdict that the accused committed the act or made the omission that formed the basis of the offence with which the accused is charged but is not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder. (verdict de non-responsabilité criminelle pour cause de troubles mentaux)
@ref s 672.1(1) "verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder" (src:13329)
GIVEN `the verdict is that the accused committed the act or made the omission that formed the basis of the offence with which the accused is charged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the verdict is that the accused is not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.1(1) verdict of not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder` MEANS
    IF `the verdict is that the accused committed the act or made the omission that formed the basis of the offence with which the accused is charged` AND `the verdict is that the accused is not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a verdict that the accused committed the act or made the omission that formed the basis of the offence with which the accused is charged but is not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder"

§ `Section 672.1(2) -- Reference: the Attorney General of a province read as the Attorney General of Canada`

-- 672.1(2): for the purposes of the listed provisions, in respect of a territory or proceedings commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of
-- that Government, a reference to the Attorney General of a province shall be read as a reference to the Attorney General of Canada. A rule of reading: it operates on which provision is being read.
-- src:13330 | Reference
-- src:13331 | (2) For the purposes of subsections 672.5(3) and (5), paragraph 672.86(1)(b) and subsections 672.86(2) and (2.1), 672.88(2) and 672.89(2), in respect of a territory or proceedings commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada and conducted by or on behalf of that Government, a reference to the Attorney General of a province shall be read as a reference to the Attorney General of Canada.
@ref s 672.1(2) (src:13330-13331)
DECLARE `s 672.1(2) provision being read` IS ONE OF
    `s 672.1(2) subsection 672.5(3)`
    `s 672.1(2) subsection 672.5(5)`
    `s 672.1(2) paragraph 672.86(1)(b)`
    `s 672.1(2) subsection 672.86(2)`
    `s 672.1(2) subsection 672.86(2.1)`
    `s 672.1(2) subsection 672.88(2)`
    `s 672.1(2) subsection 672.89(2)`
    `s 672.1(2) a provision not listed in subsection 672.1(2)`

@ref s 672.1(2) (src:13330-13331)
GIVEN provision IS A `s 672.1(2) provision being read`
      `the matter is in respect of a territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings were commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada and are conducted by or on behalf of that Government` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.1(2) a reference to the Attorney General of a province is read as a reference to the Attorney General of Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF provision EQUALS `s 672.1(2) a provision not listed in subsection 672.1(2)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of subsections 672.5(3) and (5)"
        IF `the matter is in respect of a territory` OR `the proceedings were commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada and are conducted by or on behalf of that Government` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a territory or proceedings commenced at the instance of the Government of Canada"
